    "blogtextliquid_LBJgtB": {
      "type": "editorial--blog-text-liquid",
      "custom_css": [],
      "name": "Blog Text Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "text_content": "<p>An American summer starts the second school lets out and does not fully quit until the first pumpkin spice sign appears in September. It is a season defined by sensory memory: lake docks warmed by the sun, salt spray clinging to your hair after an afternoon in the surf, and cold lemonade sweating on a patio table.</p><p>Summer fragrance is unique because warmth turns the volume up on everything. Heat lifts scent molecules off your skin with incredible speed, carrying them further on the breeze while simultaneously testing their longevity.</p>"
      }
    },
