    "blogtextliquid_ra7Awx": {
      "type": "editorial--blog-text-liquid",
      "custom_css": [],
      "name": "Blog Text Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "text_content": "<p>Wearing fragrance in July and August requires an intentional shift in notes. Heavy vanillas and winter ambers that felt so comforting in December become suffocating when the temperature climbs past 85 degrees.</p><p>Summer calls for effervescent citrus, crisp aquatics, and sun-drenched woods that radiate effortless refreshment. Here is how to curate your summer scent rotation so you smell crisp from morning beach walks to sunset rooftop gatherings.</p>"
      }
    },
    "blocks_ji7beH": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "blog_editorial_text_section_zNd6WG": {
          "type": "blog--editorial-text-section",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Coastal Aquatics vs High-Desert Woods",
            "heading_size": 42,
            "heading_size_mobile": 28,
            "heading_line_height": 1.1,
            "heading_color": "#1A1816",
            "heading_margin_bottom": 30,
            "heading_margin_bottom_mobile": 25,
            "column_1_text": "<p>Coastal aquatics capture the exhilarating rush of the ocean. Featuring marine ozone, sea salt, grapefruit, and driftwood accords, these scents feel like diving into cold Atlantic water on a scorching afternoon.</p><p>They are light, crisp, and completely inoffensive, making them the ultimate daytime companion for backyard barbecues, tennis courts, and boardwalk strolls.</p>",
            "column_2_text": "<p>High-desert woods take summer freshness in an earthier, more rugged direction. Think sunbaked cedar, wild juniper, vetiver, and crushed pine needles underfoot.</p><p>These aromatic profiles have superior heat tolerance because their woody base notes anchor volatile citrus compounds, projecting with dry, confident elegance as the summer sun sets.</p>",
            "body_size": 17,
            "body_size_mobile": 15,
            "body_line_height": 1.9,
            "body_color": "#2D2A26",
            "paragraph_spacing": 20,
            "column_gap": 55,
            "column_gap_mobile": 30,
            "max_width": 1100,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "background_color": "#FAF8F5",
            "padding_top": 60,
            "padding_bottom": 60,
            "padding_horizontal": 40,
            "padding_top_mobile": 40,
            "padding_bottom_mobile": 40,
            "padding_horizontal_mobile": 20
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "blog_editorial_text_section_zNd6WG"
      ],
      "name": "Editorial text section",
      "settings": {}
