    "1778690749e24fd023": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "blog_narrative_content_9nTtAA": {
          "type": "blog--narrative-content",
          "settings": {
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "max_width": 1100,
            "section_padding": 60,
            "background_color": "#FAF8F5",
            "heading": "<p>Cool Alpine: a cold drink you can wear</p>",
            "heading_size": 42,
            "heading_color": "#1A1816",
            "heading_spacing": 25,
            "box_color": "#1C1917",
            "box_radius": 15,
            "box_padding": 45,
            "box_spacing": 35,
            "box_paragraph_1": "<p>Some scents just feel like immediate relief, and <strong>Cool Alpine</strong> (inspired by Silver Mountain Water by Creed) is at the top of that list. Opening with crisp green tea, bergamot, and blackcurrant, it evokes glacial mountain streams and clean alpine breezes.</p><p>For an equally versatile summer staple, <strong>Marine</strong> (inspired by Bleu de Chanel) combines peppermint and citrus with clean cedar and incense, delivering fresh, effortless confidence.</p><p>If you prefer an intriguing green profile, <strong>Eternal Verde</strong> (inspired by Hacivat by Nishane) balances smoky pineapple and oakmoss for an unforgettable summer signature.</p>",
            "box_paragraph_2": "",
            "box_paragraph_3": "",
            "box_text_color": "#F5EFE6",
            "box_text_size": 17,
            "box_text_line_height": 1.9,
            "paragraph_spacing": 20,
            "subheading": "<p>Luminous Wonder & Fate for summer evenings</p>",
            "subheading_size": 42,
            "subheading_color": "#1A1816",
            "subheading_spacing": 40,
            "bottom_text": "<p>When daytime heat yields to cool evening breezes, reach for <strong>Luminous Wonder</strong> (inspired by J'Adore by Dior) or <strong>Fate</strong> (inspired by Chance EDP). Their sparkling solar florals and white amber bases radiate warmth on sun-kissed skin without feeling dense.</p><p>American summer has a rhythm: hot afternoons, warm evenings, and scents that carry through both.</p>",
            "bottom_text_size": 17,
            "bottom_text_color": "#2D2A26",
            "bottom_text_line_height": 1.9
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "blog_narrative_content_9nTtAA"
      ],
      "settings": {}
    },
