        "blog_editorial_callout_section_m8PFU4": {
          "type": "blog--editorial-callout-section",
          "settings": {
            "container_width": 1100,
            "left_column_width": 45,
            "right_column_width": 55,
            "column_gap": 50,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "heading": "What this means when you are shopping",
            "heading_font": "serif",
            "heading_size": 42,
            "mobile_heading_size": 28,
            "heading_color": "#1A1816",
            "heading_indent": 0,
            "mobile_heading_indent": 0,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/ChatGPT_Image_Jul_11_2026_02_29_17_PM.png",
            "image_max_width": 500,
            "heading_image_gap": 16,
            "mobile_heading_image_gap": 20,
            "body_text": "<p>A few small moves make a tremendous difference in summer. Always apply fragrance immediately after stepping out of the shower and applying an unscented light moisturizer, which seals hydration into your skin.</p><p>Never leave your perfume bottles in the glove compartment or on a sunny windowsill—UV rays and excessive heat will degrade the delicate citrus top notes in weeks. Keep your bottles in a cool drawer.</p>",
            "body_font": "system_ui_n4",
            "body_size": 17,
            "mobile_body_size": 15,
            "body_color": "#2D2A26",
            "paragraph_spacing": 20,
            "mobile_paragraph_spacing": 15,
            "text_vertical_offset": 0,
